Looking at the metrics, the 0.9 success rate suggests ~10% of test cases fail — likely because all greedy orderings fail to fit models, raising ValueError. A fallback that still returns a placement (even if imperfect) would recover those cases. I'll also add a "most free memory" tie-breaking fallback.

```python
GPU_MEM_SIZE = 80  # GB

